  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 123 AM CDT Tue Aug 11 2026\n\nDecreasing moisture and building high pressure will keep rain \nchances to a minimal at least through Thursday. Some weaknesses will \ntravel around the south side of the ridge, but these will remain \nmainly south of the area, and with PWAT values not much above normal \nvalues, think the best we can see is an isolated sea breeze shower, \nbut meso models not even suggesting that for the next few days. By \nFriday the ridge does shift a bit northward allowing disturbances to \nget a little closer. Moisture will increase a bit Friday, but not \nsubstantially and will maintain only 20% PoPs. \n\nSeasonal temperatures are expected with a very slight uptick toward \nthe second half of the week. Highs will be above 100 daily over the \nRio Grande Plains and in the 90s east. Heat index values on Tuesday \nmay briefly top 110 for a few locations, but this should be limited. \nWednesday and Thursday have a better chance to have heat advisory \nlevel conditions.",
